# Installed as a snippet inside /etc/apparmor.d/local/usr.sbin.libvirtd.
#
# libvirtd probes and launches the emulator itself, and the stock profile
# allows that only for /usr/bin/*. Without this, `virsh define` on a domain
# naming the Starling QEMU fails at probe time with
#
#   cannot execute binary /usr/lib/starling/qemu/bin/qemu-system-x86_64:
#   Permission denied
#
# which reads as a file-permission problem and is not one — the binary is
# 0755 and every directory above it is traversable.
/usr/lib/starling/qemu/bin/qemu-system-x86_64 PUx,
